{"id":"5bf03488a780ddc7f70b5210","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/15/houthi-missiles-strike-aden-yemen","published_at":"2026-10-16T00:27:21Z","collected_at":"2026-10-16T00:50:13.666828Z","title":"Houthi missiles strike Yemen presidential palace, killing five","text":"Smoke billows from the presidential palace following an attack by the Houthis, according to government officials, in Aden, Yemen, on Thursday. Photograph: Social Media/Reuters View image in fullscreen Smoke billows from the presidential palace following an attack by the Houthis, according to government officials, in Aden, Yemen, on Thursday. Photograph: Social Media/Reuters Yemen Houthi missiles strike Yemen presidential palace, killing five Attack was the first on Aden’s Al-Maashiq palace ⁠in the latest fighting between ​the Iran-aligned Houthis and Saudi Arabia Guardian staff and agencies Thu 15 Oct 2026 20.27 EDT First published on Thu 15 Oct 2026 16.00 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google Yemen’s Houthis fired missiles at the presidential palace complex in the southern city of Aden on Thursday, killing five people, the government said, as the Saudi-led coalition listed dozens of Houthi attacks on Saudi infrastructure in ⁠recent weeks. The attack was the first on Aden’s Al-Maashiq palace ⁠in the current conflict between ​the Iran-aligned Houthis and Saudi Arabia . The palace is the seat of Yemen’s Saudi-backed and internationally recognised government. Yemen’s prime minister,","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/234bda518d7c94db638f08b702b7928133eada55/0_219_1164_931/master/1164.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Guardian staff and agencies","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"33eb14b926798c2664d5762e75ef02127b85f7e2c1ec5e14cd5b07f59115464a","original_text_chars":4819,"original_html_chars":16766,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/15/houthi-missiles-strike-aden-yemen","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/15/houthi-missiles-strike-aden-yemen"}}}
{"id":"afd1939160425264b8378f4b","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/15/donald-trump-midterms-rallies-iran-ukraine-starlink-intelligence-fuel-gas-cost-of-living-latest-news-updates","published_at":"2026-10-16T00:36:47Z","collected_at":"2026-10-16T00:50:17.644999Z","title":"Pentagon says Trump and Hegseth ‘completely aligned’ on decision to cancel livestream of firing squad execution – live","text":"Pentagon spokesperson says pair spoke before announcement canceling plan to broadcast execution of Nidal Hasan, who killed 13 people at Fort Hood Q&A: Our reporters answered your questions about the US economy and the midterm elections Sign up for the Breaking News US email The US government could spend hundreds of thousands of dollars on a media campaign in South Africa to figure out why more white Afrikaners are not applying to become refugees to the US , as Donald Trump had hoped. State department officials, according to an August proposal seen by the Guardian, outlined a roughly $335,000 research and advertising effort after applications to the refugee program “trended lower than expected” since Afrikaners were allowed to apply directly online in November 2025. The document, written by the US mission in South Africa with a department research unit for the embassy in Pretoria, admits officials know little about why. Continue reading...","html":"","media":[],"author":"Robert Mackey (now); Gabrielle Canon, Shrai Popat, Lucy Campbell, Shannon Ho and Siraj Datoo (earlier)","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"73bdf6016632abb03e371be94b5ad5beff4bfeb22018a53cd145227a316e8093","original_text_chars":952,"original_html_chars":2491,"text_truncated":false,"media_count":0,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/15/donald-trump-midterms-rallies-iran-ukraine-starlink-intelligence-fuel-gas-cost-of-living-latest-news-updates","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/15/donald-trump-midterms-rallies-iran-ukraine-starlink-intelligence-fuel-gas-cost-of-living-latest-news-updates"}}}
